{"name":"Abbey Road","hex":"#a79f92","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"abbey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The office or dominion of an abbot or abbess. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A monastery or society of people, secluded from the world and devoted to religion and celibacy, which is headed by an abbot or abbess; also, the monastic building or buildings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abbey"},{"term":"road","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A way used for travelling between places, originally one wide enough to allow foot passengers and horses to travel, now (US) usually one surfaced with asphalt or concrete and designed to accommodate many vehicles travelling in both directions. In the UK both senses are heard: a country road is the same as a country lane. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Roads in general as a means of travel, especially by motor vehicle."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At the venue of the opposing team or competitor; on the road.","Of or pertaining to a road bike."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/road"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abbey Road","blocks":[{"text":"Abbey Road is the eleventh studio album by the English rock band the Beatles, released on 26 September 1969 by Apple Records. It is the last album the group recorded – although Let It Be had mostly been recorded earlier, its release was delayed due to production issues. Abbey Road was mostly recorded in April, July and August 1969, and topped the record charts in both the United States and the United Kingdom. A double A-side single from the album, \"Something\" / \"Come Together\", was released in October, which also topped the charts in the US."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/The_Beatles_Abbey_Road_album_cover.jpg/330px-The_Beatles_Abbey_Road_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbey_Road"},{"title":"Abbey Road (ward)","blocks":[{"text":"Abbey Road is an electoral ward in the City of Westminster. The ward was first used in the 2002 elections. It returns three councillors to Westminster City Council."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbey_Road_(ward)"},{"title":"Abbey","blocks":[{"text":"An abbey is a type of monastery used by members of a religious order under the governance of an abbot or abbess. Abbeys provide a complex of buildings and land for religious activities, work, and housing of Christian or Buddhist monks and nuns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Senanquecloister.jpg/330px-Senanquecloister.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbey"},{"title":"Road","blocks":[{"text":"A road is a thoroughfare from one place to another, primarily used for movement of traffic. Many roads are paved."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg/330px-Erlangen_Bundesautobahn_73_Auffahrt_Luftbild-20230422-RM-165734.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/TG12345_Mk.II_desk_%281970s%29_and_Microphones%2C_Abbey_Road_Studios.jpg/500px-TG12345_Mk.II_desk_%281970s%29_and_Microphones%2C_Abbey_Road_Studios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/TG12345_Mk.II_desk_%281970s%29_and_Microphones%2C_Abbey_Road_Studios.jpg/1280px-TG12345_Mk.II_desk_%281970s%29_and_Microphones%2C_Abbey_Road_Studios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/TG12345_Mk.II_desk_%281970s%29_and_Micro